{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-kimi-k3-max-full200-2026-09-29","prediction_set_name":"kimi-k3-max-full200-2026-09-29","paper_id":"2601.21764","judge_input_sha256":"3174c7c207c96f21ed2f6c69992601ad891b797353675de5e0dda6c7cfd6c548","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2601.21764:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"no_substantive_overlap","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.21764:I001:U002","2601.21764:I001:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is the use of unsigned powers and the missing signed duality map for arbitrary real q with sign-indefinite residuals. ISSUE-001 concerns an inverse operator-norm inference from diagonal dominance; it does not diagnose the loss formula or gradient identity.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.21764:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.21764:I002:U001","2601.21764:I002:U002","2601.21764:I002:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is transposing Jacobian limits before forming the convex combination, which loses the row-diagonal-dominance premise and omits the needed regrouping argument. ISSUE-001 addresses a separate Gershgorin-to-inverse-norm inference and its repair does not recognize the transpose/order-of-combination defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.21764:I007","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.21764:I007:U001","2601.21764:I007:U002"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is an incompatible six-dimensional PDE declaration versus five-dimensional samples, stencils, and network inputs, making the experiment non-instantiable. ISSUE-002 concerns an incorrect time-dependent variable transform and does not diagnose dimensional consistency of the experiment.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.21764:I008","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.21764:I008:U001","2601.21764:I008:U002","2601.21764:I008:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U010"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is omission of the 1/sqrt(5) normalization in the implemented Hamiltonian, changing the advection speed. ISSUE-003 concerns a missing amplification factor in an implicit time-stepping stability estimate and does not recognize the Hamiltonian scaling error.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_req